From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pankraz76 <punkratz1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:58:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 10055: Assembler: do not match empty labels in numeric
 terminals

Assembler: skip symbol table lookup for empty names

When a numeric operand is expected but the input has no label
characters at that position (e.g. right after "[" or "#"),
AssemblyNumericTerminal.match looks up the empty string.
SymbolTable.getSymbols("") returns every default-named symbol
(FUN_xxxxxxxx), since those are stored without a name. Each became a
zero-width symbol token, forking one parse branch per function. On
large programs this made every keystroke in Patch Instruction take
seconds, and it let incomplete input such as "ldr x0,[x1, #]" be
accepted with an arbitrary function address as the operand.

Skip the symbol table in AssemblyNumericSymbols.chooseAll and
chooseBySpace when the name is empty. Equates and language labels are
plain maps and need no special handling.

AArch64, 300k labels + 50k default-named functions, median of 5 runs
after 2 warm-ups:
  parseLine("ldr x0, [")    1687.7 ms -> 2.3 ms
  parseLine("ldr x0,[x1, ") 1316.8 ms -> 2.6 ms

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MTr23yotYR4n4votGs7j1e
